Passages 1 and 3 give different current Generalmusikdirektors: Thomas Guggeis since 2023/24 versus Sebastian Weigle since 2008/09. Both could be true at different times, since Weigle served from 2008 to 2023 and Guggeis took over in 2023. But "this has been" in the present tense implies a single current holder, so they conflict about who currently holds the post. Passage 3 is the outdated one, and Guggeis is the current GMD, so passage 3 is more likely the misinformation. This is arguably temporal, but I am treating it as a contradiction.

Passage 2 says Mengelberg directed the concerts in 1907–1920 and that Hindemith was concertmaster from 1915 to 1922. Those details do not conflict with the other passages. Passage 0 is also compatible with the rest.

